cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Rootline, please cite it as below."
title: "Rootline: an open benchmark and replay app for evidence-grounded AI diagnosis of microservice failures"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: flotrpy
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Flotrpy/RootLine"
abstract: >-
  Rootline is an open, reproducible benchmark and replay app for
  evidence-grounded AI diagnosis of microservice failures. It measures which
  telemetry signals free and open models need, whether they can tell network
  faults from application faults, how easily misleading evidence fools them,
  and whether their proposed fixes actually restore service.
keywords:
  - root cause analysis
  - observability
  - OpenTelemetry
  - large language models
  - benchmark
